cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.'
title: 'IELTS API: a free, no-authentication REST API and open dataset for IELTS preparation research'
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-09-05'
abstract: >-
  IELTS API is an open, dependency-free TypeScript REST API that publishes
  machine-readable IELTS preparation data: 4,174 headwords extracted from the
  Cambridge IELTS volumes 1-22 vocabulary lists, condensed analytic band
  descriptors for Speaking and Writing across bands 0-9, indicative score
  concordances for CEFR, TOEFL iBT, the Cambridge English Scale, PTE Academic
  and the Duolingo English Test, exhaustive raw-score to band-score conversion
  tables for the Listening and Reading papers, the complete Listening and
  Reading question-type taxonomy, test-format blueprints for all six papers,
  Writing and Speaking task banks, and a curated index of an open IELTS
  research corpus. Every raw-score boundary records whether it is reproduced
  from agreeing public sources or extrapolated, and boundaries where public
  tables disagree carry the competing value, so a study can report its
  sensitivity to the choice of table. Every endpoint is free of charge,
  requires no authentication, returns a uniform JSON envelope with a stable
  ETag, and is covered by a test suite with 100% statement, branch, function
  and line coverage. The API is designed for reproducible second-language
  assessment research: responses are deterministic, versioned and citable, and
  the service publishes its own paper, PDF full text and citation metadata in
  nine reference-manager formats.
keywords:
  - IELTS
  - English for Academic Purposes
  - second language assessment
  - vocabulary
  - band descriptors
  - score concordance
  - raw score conversion
  - question types
  - language testing
  - open data
  - REST API
  - TypeScript
